WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.780
The Amazing Pole Vaulter? The Mysterious Man With&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:08.460
1,000 False IDs? These aren't Marvel&nbsp;
characters; they're Marvel actors.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.060
Though it was a bit of a surprise&nbsp;
when it was first announced,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:17.820
Woody Harrelson wound up playing the villain&nbsp;
Cletus Kasady aka Carnage in 2021's "Venom:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:22.620
Let There Be Carnage." He also has a bit of&nbsp;
history when it comes to the law. In 1982,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.360
as detailed in an interview with The Hollywood&nbsp;
Reporter, Harrelson was arrested for jaywalking,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:32.340
and things got out of hand. As Harrelson&nbsp;
recalled, he and an unnamed friend were the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:36.240
victims of police brutality after being&nbsp;
stopped for jaywalking. The actor said,

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:40.440
"It was so brutal, the way they were&nbsp;
handling me. A bunch of students gathered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:44.280
around and were complaining to the cops,&nbsp;
and the cops were vicious to them, too."

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:49.080
According to Harrelson, the incident culminated&nbsp;
in him being maced to prevent him from fleeing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:54.540
the scene, before he was taken to jail with&nbsp;
six separate charges against him. He added,

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:58.560
"That was a real eye-opener — and an&nbsp;
eye-closer at the same time because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.980
it really f---ed my eyes. I had to&nbsp;
wear sunglasses for a long time."

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:07.020
Though this incident was by no means the last&nbsp;
of his encounters with the law, the three-time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:12.720
Academy Award nominee, long-time cannabis&nbsp;
activist, and vegan lives a less eventful life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:18.059
these days. Hopefully, he manages to stay out of&nbsp;
the kind of limelight that leads to more mugshots.

00:01:18.059 --> 00:01:20.940
"If you're gonna treat me like&nbsp;
a baby, I'm gonna act like one."

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:25.380
Despite the fact that Josh Brolin's&nbsp;
first foray into the world of comic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:28.560
book adaptations with "Jonah&nbsp;
Hex" was largely unsuccessful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.540
he was clearly not turned off the genre. He&nbsp;
later portrayed two major Marvel characters:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:38.460
Cable in "Deadpool 2" and The&nbsp;
Avengers' ultimate foe, Thanos.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:43.320
Despite earlier encounters with law enforcement,&nbsp;
the actor's experience with mugshots didn't begin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:48.180
until 2008. He was arrested for interfering&nbsp;
with an arrest outside a bar in Shreveport,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:51.240
LA along with Marvel co-star&nbsp;
Jeffrey Wright. While neither&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:55.440
actor has given much insight into the&nbsp;
event, Brolin did state in W Magazine,

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:59.820
"It was nice to be in jail knowing that&nbsp;
I hadn't done anything wrong. And it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:03.300
was maddening to be in jail knowing&nbsp;
that I hadn't done anything wrong."

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:08.280
In 2013, the actor had a second encounter with&nbsp;
police in Santa Monica just before midnight on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:12.540
New Year's Eve while intoxicated and pole&nbsp;
vaulting down the street near his home.&nbsp;

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:15.120
According to Santa Monica Police Lt. Darrell Lowe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:20.220
Brolin was booked and then released approximately&nbsp;
6 hours later once he had sobered up. The actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:24.600
has since stated that it was a significant&nbsp;
moment for him. Via The Guardian, he said,

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:29.880
"I realized that I was on a destructive path.&nbsp;
I knew that I had to change and mature."

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:33.480
While Jeffrey Wright is a newer&nbsp;
addition to the Marvel canon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:38.280
his relationship with fellow Marvel veteran&nbsp;
Josh Brolin goes back far beyond his time in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:43.860
the MCU. He plays the Watcher, a cosmic being&nbsp;
who serves as the narrator of "What If...?"

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.949
"There is still hope for this universe."

00:02:46.949 --> 00:02:51.540
As previously mentioned, Brolin and Wright&nbsp;
were arrested in Shreveport, LA, outside of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:56.880
Stray Cat bar where the pair had been attending&nbsp;
a wrap party for their film "W" back in 2008.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:01.200
Following a report of cast and crew members&nbsp;
refusing to leave despite being asked,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.220
the police were summoned. When Brolin and&nbsp;
Wright stepped in to attempt to diffuse the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:10.800
situation they were restrained on charges of&nbsp;
interfering with an officer, via Action News 5.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.640
Witness accounts along with a video&nbsp;
of the arrest which was released by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:19.080
the Associated Press suggest possible&nbsp;
police misconduct. TMZ reports at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:22.740
time indicated that Wright tasered&nbsp;
multiple times and pepper sprayed.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:27.420
Cited witness statements claim foul,&nbsp;
racially-fueled language being used by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:32.220
police officers. Unfortunately, despite multiple&nbsp;
witness reports, the Shreveport Police Department&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:37.440
ultimately deemed that their officers had&nbsp;
responded with professionalism. Also, none of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:42.903
the fellow officers who had previously attested to&nbsp;
witnessing the tirade had officially come forward.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:47.940
While the star of the original "Blade" series&nbsp;
will not be returning for the MCU reboot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:52.620
Wesley Snipes' place in Marvel history&nbsp;
will never be forgotten. Snipes has had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:57.600
several encounters with law enforcement, but&nbsp;
it wasn't until 2008 that the "U.S. Marshals"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:02.160
actor had his mugshot taken by none other&nbsp;
than the U.S. Marshals Service themselves.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:09.000
After his arrest, the actor faced charges for&nbsp;
failing to file tax returns between 1999 and 2004,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:13.620
a period wherein he had accrued nearly&nbsp;
$40 million. Though he offered to pay&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:20.700
approximately $842,000 of his $23.5 million&nbsp;
debt, Snipes was fined $5 million and given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:24.960
a three-year prison sentence, according to&nbsp;
People. He was released from prison in 2013,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:30.360
after which he quickly resumed his acting career,&nbsp;
appearing in films such as "Chi-Raq," "Dolomite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:34.320
Is My Name," and "Coming 2 America."&nbsp;
The latter film would see him reprise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:39.000
his role from the 1980s cult comedy classic&nbsp;
"Coming to America" starring Eddie Murphy.&nbsp;

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:44.340
In 2020, Snipes' arrest re-entered the public's&nbsp;
focus due to the apparent hypocrisy of the U.S.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:48.360
Government not arresting former President&nbsp;
Donald Trump after accusations of tax&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:52.260
evasion. The actor's arrest and federal&nbsp;
prison time were seen in a new light,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:56.880
with many people calling for apologies to be&nbsp;
made, including author Sam J. Miller, who wrote,

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:00.780
"Wesley Snipes and Lauryn Hill&nbsp;
had their careers destroyed (OH&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:03.577
AND THEY WENT TO JAIL) for failing to pay taxes."

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:07.680
The original Rhodey to RDJ's Tony&nbsp;
Stark, "Iron Man" co-star Terrence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:12.420
Howard has had a tumultuous personal life.&nbsp;
The Academy Award-nominated actor had his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:16.080
mugshot captured twice, both times&nbsp;
related to an assault on a woman.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:19.980
In the year 2000, Howard was arrested&nbsp;
after a flight attendant accused him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:23.760
of grabbing her during a disagreement&nbsp;
surrounding the "fasten seat belt" sign,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:28.920
according to ABC News. While charges were not&nbsp;
pursued after his 2000 arrest, the details&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:35.580
behind his 2001 mugshot are a bit more complex, as&nbsp;
cited by The Chicago Tribune and The Smoking Gun.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:39.840
In 2001, Howard admitted to striking&nbsp;
his first wife, Lori McCommas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:42.060
prior to their divorce. He&nbsp;
stated, via Rolling Stone,

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:47.100
"She was talking to me real strong, and I lost&nbsp;
my mind and slapped her in front of the kids."

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:51.900
The Whitemarsh Police Department report details&nbsp;
the argument that immediately preceded the event,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:55.080
wherein the actor warned over&nbsp;
the phone, per The Smoking Gun,

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:59.640
"Don't disrespect me by hanging up on&nbsp;
me or I'll come over and hurt you."

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:03.780
McCommas still hung up. She then called&nbsp;
911 afraid of what Howard might do. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:07.260
attack ended when Howard's brother&nbsp;
entered McCommas' home. The brother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:12.060
saw Howard storm out of his house to go to&nbsp;
the victim's house and followed. In 2002,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:16.169
the actor pleaded guilty to disorderly&nbsp;
conduct in relation to the incident.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:21.780
In 2003's "Hulk," Nick Nolte portrayed&nbsp;
David Banner, the genius who served as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:25.740
both father and origin story for&nbsp;
Eric Bana's Bruce Banner. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:30.120
the film might not be the Hulk's definitive&nbsp;
appearance, Nolte's depiction of the doomed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:33.780
researcher remains the only iteration&nbsp;
of the character within the modern MCU.

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:39.300
Nolte's first significant run-in with authorities&nbsp;
occurred in 1961 when the three-time Academy Award&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:44.760
nominee was arrested in Omaha. This was following&nbsp;
a bizarre series of events involving a pack of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:50.280
1,000 falsified IDs falling out of a nonfunctional&nbsp;
hearse. Of the event, Nolte has stated,&nbsp;

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:53.880
"I don't think it was an intentional&nbsp;
criminal act. It was stupidity."

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:57.840
While he was convicted and&nbsp;
sentenced to a 45-year prison&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:01.140
stint, the sentence was ultimately&nbsp;
suspended, according to Esquire.

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:05.820
In 2002 — almost exactly one decade&nbsp;
after being declared People's Sexiest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:10.080
Man Alive – Nolte had his photo snapped&nbsp;
following his arrest for driving under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:13.080
the influence. Nolte described&nbsp;
the event in his memoir, writing,

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:16.500
"I was a mess and driving on the&nbsp;
Pacific Coast Highway. I'm told&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:21.600
six drivers called 911 to report a big sedan&nbsp;
weaving on the wrong side of the road."

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:26.760
Despite significant evidence to the contrary,&nbsp;
Nolte himself has claimed that the photo in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:31.683
question was closer to being a souvenir for&nbsp;
one of the officers present at the station.

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:36.960
Hollywood superstar Nicolas Cage was already&nbsp;
a well-seasoned actor by the time he revved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:42.000
up audiences in 2007's "Ghost Rider." This&nbsp;
was a role he committed to with the exact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:46.800
amount of hyperactive enthusiasm he has been&nbsp;
famous for since his arrival on the Hollywood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:52.560
scene way back in 1981. His self-branded&nbsp;
"Nouveau Shamanic" style of acting has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:57.360
earned him one Academy Award, and there's&nbsp;
no sign of him slowing down any time soon.

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:01.920
Though there have been some false claims within&nbsp;
Cage's legal history, the actor definitely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:06.600
interacted with law enforcement when a mugshot was&nbsp;
taken after the actor was arrested in New Orleans.

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:10.080
During what appeared to be a domestic&nbsp;
dispute on the street, onlookers flagged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:14.580
down police outside a residence in the French&nbsp;
Quarter in 2011. Upon arriving at the scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:18.780
the responding officer noticed immediately&nbsp;
that Cage was heavily intoxicated.

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:22.560
"Tell you the truth I'm a little shaky right now."

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:28.020
He then escorted him down to central lock up,&nbsp;
according to Reuters. The actor was photographed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:32.880
and processed before being bailed out by none&nbsp;
other than Duane "Dog the Bounty Hunter" Chapman.

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:37.260
After the case was reviewed by the District&nbsp;
Attorney's Office it was deemed that there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:41.340
was insufficient evidence to charge Cage&nbsp;
with a criminal offense. According to CNN,

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:45.240
"The District Attorney's Office did&nbsp;
not give Nic Cage any breaks because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:50.451
of his status. At the same time, we are not&nbsp;
going to judge him more harshly, either."

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:55.560
Marvel's favorite leading man Robert&nbsp;
Downey Jr. first started portraying Tony&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.560 --> 00:09:00.720
Stark in 2008's "Iron Man," the film that&nbsp;
marked the official beginning of the MCU.

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:06.660
Not entirely unlike his on-screen bad-boy&nbsp;
persona, RDJ himself has been arrested on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:11.880
multiple occasions, primarily in association&nbsp;
with drug-related charges. His long struggle with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:17.280
addiction and recovery has been covered many times&nbsp;
over. Some of his stories can be told with a more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:22.380
tongue-in-cheek tone these days, like his arrest&nbsp;
for smoking cannabis in Disneyland. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:27.360
the arrests associated with the actor's three&nbsp;
most accessible mugshots are more serious.

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:31.740
In 1996, he was arrested for&nbsp;
possession of cocaine and heroin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:37.140
as well as a handgun. Following another arrest&nbsp;
two weeks later involving breaking and entering,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:42.420
RDJ entered the beginning of his recovery&nbsp;
process. According to The LA Times this included&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.420 --> 00:09:47.760
two in-custody programs, two residential&nbsp;
programs, and two rehabilitation programs.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:54.060
Following his failure to submit to three separate&nbsp;
drug tests in 1999, the actor was arrested and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:59.340
sentenced to three years in prison, where his&nbsp;
first mugshot was captured. The subsequent two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:04.980
mugshots were taken following similar drug-related&nbsp;
arrests in 2000 and 2001, respectively.

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:10.560
Downey Jr. has since stated that he's been sober&nbsp;
since 2012. He said in an interview with Oprah,

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:15.468
"For me, I just happened to be in a&nbsp;
situation the very last time and I said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.468 --> 00:10:18.179
'You know what? I don't think&nbsp;
I can continue doing this.'"

00:10:18.179 --> 00:10:20.356
"﻿Don’t do anything I would do,&nbsp;
and definitely don't do anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.356 --> 00:10:25.207
I wouldn't do. There's a little grey area&nbsp;
in there, and that's where you operate."﻿

00:10:25.207 --> 00:10:28.740
While Mickey Rourke has expressed regrets&nbsp;
about his role in the Marvel Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:34.080
his portrayal of Ivan Vanko — aka Whiplash&nbsp;
— was an interesting introduction to "Iron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:38.460
Man." As it turns out, Rourke himself is no&nbsp;
stranger to encounters with the law. Though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.460 --> 00:10:43.080
his 1994 charge of resisting arrest and&nbsp;
allegation of spousal abuse came first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:47.880
the arrest associated with this&nbsp;
mugshot didn't occur until 2007.

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:52.140
On November 8th, 2007, the actor was&nbsp;
arrested for driving under the influence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:55.680
following a traffic stop attributed&nbsp;
to an illegal U-turn on his motorized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:59.760
scooter in Miami Beach. Per Reuters, the&nbsp;
arresting officer said of the incident,

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:02.700
"[Rourke had] bloodshot, watery eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:06.360
slurred speech and a strong&nbsp;
odor of an alcoholic beverage."

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:10.800
He was placed under arrest, even though&nbsp;
the actor denied the allegations at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:15.900
time being. Though the former boxer's transition&nbsp;
into Hollywood life and his history with substance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:20.100
use and personal struggles are known to have&nbsp;
taken a toll on him, he claims to have found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:26.280
means of recovery in recent years. He publicly&nbsp;
thanked his agent David A. Unger, his priest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:31.920
and weekly sessions with a psychiatrist for aiding&nbsp;
him in his recovery and subsequent comeback.

